---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Mauricio Meza — mechanical designer and mechatronics engineer bridging precision manufacturing with robotics."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <!-- Avatar -->
    <div class="flex items-center gap-6 mb-10">
      <div class="w-24 h-24 rounded-full bg-surface border-2 border-accent/40 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
        <span class="text-2xl font-bold text-accent">MM</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-primary">Mauricio Meza</h1>
        <p class="text-muted font-mono text-sm mt-1">Mechanical Designer · Mechatronics Engineer · Phoenix, AZ</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Career arc -->
    <div class="mb-12 prose prose-invert prose-sm max-w-none prose-p:text-muted prose-p:leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        I started as an electrical engineering graduate from ITESCA in Mexico — BSEE in Mechatronics, class of 2013 —
        and spent the next decade working across automation, controls, and eventually precision mechanical design.
        The work that stuck was physical: designing the fixtures that hold parts at the right angle,
        the assemblies that absorb vibration without failing, the tooling that keeps a manufacturing line running.
      </p>
      <p>
        After moving to Phoenix, I built seven years of industrial design experience across HVAC, aerospace,
        retail display, and emergency response industries. I hold a CSWP certification and have shipped
        designs that went into production — not just simulations. Along the way I kept pulling at the
        robotics and autonomy thread: ROS 2, Python, control theory, perception.
      </p>
      <p>
        Now I'm closing the loop. I'm preparing my application to ASU's MS Robotics & Autonomous Systems
        program (EE concentration, target Spring 2027) — not as a career pivot, but as the logical next
        step for an engineer who has always been interested in what happens when mechanical systems
        start to move on their own.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Education -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-mono text-muted uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">Education</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <div class="bg-surface border border-accent/20 rounded-lg p-5">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary">MS Robotics & Autonomous Systems</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted">Arizona State University — EE concentration</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-muted">Planned 2027</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface border border-accent/20 rounded-lg p-5">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary">BSEE — Mechatronics Engineering</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted">ITESCA, Mexico</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-muted">2013</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Certifications -->
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-mono text-muted uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">Certifications</h2>
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 bg-surface border border-accent/20 rounded-lg px-5 py-4">
        <img src="/images/cswp-badge.svg" alt="CSWP" class="h-8 w-8 object-contain" />
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary">Certified SolidWorks Professional (CSWP)</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted font-mono">Dassault Systèmes</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Skills grid -->
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xs font-mono text-muted uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">Skills</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-surface border border-accent/20 rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-bright uppercase mb-3">Mechanical Design</h3>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            {['SolidWorks (CSWP)', 'AutoCAD', 'GD&T', 'FEA / Simulation', 'Fixture & Tooling Design', 'Sheet Metal', 'Design Tables'].map(s => (
              <li class="text-sm text-muted">{s}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface border border-accent/20 rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-bright uppercase mb-3">Electrical / Controls</h3>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            {['PLC Programming', 'Mechatronics', 'Automation', 'Sensors & Actuators', 'Circuit Design'].map(s => (
              <li class="text-sm text-muted">{s}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface border border-accent/20 rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-bright uppercase mb-3">Software</h3>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            {['Python', 'NumPy / SciPy', 'OpenCV', 'PyTorch', 'Git', 'Linux'].map(s => (
              <li class="text-sm text-muted">{s}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface border border-accent/20 rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-bright uppercase mb-3">Robotics</h3>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            {['ROS 2', 'Control Theory', 'Kinematics', 'Point Cloud Processing (PCL)', 'LiDAR / Depth Sensors'].map(s => (
              <li class="text-sm text-muted">{s}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
